### Login to get JWT token first
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin@123456"
}

### Add Return Policy Document
POST http://localhost:5000/api/knowledge
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "title": "Company Return Policy",
  "content": "Our company has a flexible return policy designed to ensure customer satisfaction:\n\n1. Return Window: You can return any product within 30 days of purchase for a full refund.\n\n2. Condition Requirements: Items must be in original condition with all tags and packaging intact.\n\n3. Refund Processing: Once we receive your return, refunds are processed within 5-7 business days to your original payment method.\n\n4. Exceptions: Sale items and clearance products can be returned but are eligible for store credit only, not refunds.\n\n5. Shipping Costs: Original shipping costs are non-refundable. Return shipping is free if the item is defective.\n\n6. How to Return: Contact our customer service team at support@company.com or call 1-800-RETURNS to initiate a return. We'll provide you with a prepaid return label.\n\n7. Exchanges: If you prefer an exchange instead of a return, we'll ship the replacement item at no additional cost.",
  "category": "Policy",
  "source": "Company Policy Manual v2.0"
}

### Search Knowledge Base (no auth required for search)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/knowledge/search?query=return%20policy&limit=5

### Load documents to Qdrant (after adding documents)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/knowledge/load-to-qdrant
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### Get all knowledge documents
GET http://localhost:5000/api/knowledge
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
